{"timestamp":"2026-07-27T19:40:30.500Z","type":"decision","context":"proxy.ts + app/checkout/page.tsx","content":"Redirect bug fix: /checkout gate was implemented as useEffect + sessionStorage.getItem(). This runs client-side after hydration — Next.js SSR serves the full job card HTML before JS executes, so a direct navigation to /checkout with no approvalStatus set would flash the protected content before redirecting. Fixed by moving the gate to proxy.ts (Next.js 16 server-side middleware, renamed from middleware.ts). The proxy reads an approvalStatus cookie set at underwriting approval and issues a 307 redirect before any HTML is generated. Verified: curl -s -D - http://localhost:3000/checkout returns HTTP/1.1 307 with no cookie; returns 200 with cookie.","tags":["checkout-gate","proxy","redirect","ssr","bug-fix","verified"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-27T19:42:27.508Z","type":"milestone","context":"README.md","content":"README written to exact graded structure from brief: what/why/who (multi-sided — ABC Community Bank as buyer, AirConPro as integration partner, CoolAir HVAC as sub-merchant, Arnold Freeze as consumer); APIs used and why (Stripe for card path, mocked routes for underwriting and financing); run locally instructions; product decisions section including PayFac reframe, why financing was added, why stubs are stubbed, redirect bug/fix, and honest session hook limitations; what next section (multi-bank routing, async webhooks, real KYB, fraud scoring, hook discipline); builder context stated plainly and specifically.","tags":["readme","task-13","graded-deliverable"]}
